# LIBRARY: own
# f1 = read, f3 = the getter
# A read that finds a getter of the class runs it, in line or by a call. Behind it the getter, which does something, may have changed what the name finds, so nothing can be asked there.
# Under testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime the object is asked in front of the getter whether the name finds an accessor whose getter is a closure of that function. 3330 says "an accessor, answered by the function that the compiler takes a name to find".
# RUN(FRONT): walk f1 mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime
# FRONT: AskObjectAgain {{*}} key="size" function=f3 [functionIsGetter]
# FRONT: AskObjectAgain {{*}} key="reads"
# FRONT-NOT: key="size"
# RUN(EMIT): emit f1 mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime
# EMIT: = Const32(3330)
# RUN(PLAIN): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# PLAIN-NOT: AskObjectAgain
# RUN(ASKED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime
